  "content": {
    "id": "p46-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Let $Z$ have the standard normal distribution. Use these cumulative table values, given to 4 decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $P(Z\\le z)$ |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.5000 |\n| 0.7 | 0.7580 |\n| 1 | 0.8413 |\n| 1.3 | 0.9032 |\n| 1.6 | 0.9452 |\n| 2 | 0.9772 |\n| 2.4 | 0.9918 |\n| 3.9 | 1.0000 |",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p46-q2-explanation",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Explain why $P(Z>a)=1-P(Z\\le a)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The events $Z>a$ and $Z\\le a$ are complementary, so their probabilities sum to 1.",
          "worked": "Every value of $Z$ lies in exactly one of the events $Z>a$ and $Z\\le a$. Therefore $P(Z>a)+P(Z\\le a)=1$, giving $P(Z>a)=1-P(Z\\le a)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p46-q2-calculations",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "Hence find, correct to 4 decimal places:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 4,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$P(Z>0)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.5000$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z>0)&=1-P(Z\\le0)\\\\P(Z>0)&=1-0.5000\\\\P(Z>0)&=0.5000\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$P(Z>1)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.1587$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z>1)&=1-P(Z\\le1)\\\\P(Z>1)&=1-0.8413\\\\P(Z>1)&=0.1587\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$P(Z>2)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.0228$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z>2)&=1-P(Z\\le2)\\\\P(Z>2)&=1-0.9772\\\\P(Z>2)&=0.0228\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "$P(Z\\ge2.4)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.0082$",
              "worked": "Since $Z$ is continuous, $P(Z=2.4)=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge2.4)&=1-P(Z\\le2.4)\\\\P(Z\\ge2.4)&=1-0.9918\\\\P(Z\\ge2.4)&=0.0082\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 23
          },
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "$P(Z>1.3)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.0968$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z>1.3)&=1-P(Z\\le1.3)\\\\P(Z>1.3)&=1-0.9032\\\\P(Z>1.3)&=0.0968\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "g",
            "prompt": "$P(Z>0.7)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.2420$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z>0.7)&=1-P(Z\\le0.7)\\\\P(Z>0.7)&=1-0.7580\\\\P(Z>0.7)&=0.2420\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-g",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "h",
            "prompt": "$P(Z\\ge1.6)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.0548$",
              "worked": "Since $Z$ is continuous, $P(Z=1.6)=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\ge1.6)&=1-P(Z\\le1.6)\\\\P(Z\\ge1.6)&=1-0.9452\\\\P(Z\\ge1.6)&=0.0548\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 23
          },
          {
            "id": "p46-q2-h",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "$P(Z>8)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0.0000$",
              "worked": "The table gives $P(Z\\le3.9)=1.0000$ to 4 decimal places. Since $8>3.9$, $P(Z>8)$ is smaller than $P(Z>3.9)$, so $P(Z>8)=0.0000$ to 4 decimal places.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 23
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
